  body: "# Incapacity Benefit contribution-record referral\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured IB guidance
    distinguishes the DM’s contribution-condition decision from an HMRC formal decision needed when the underlying
    national insurance contribution record is disputed.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis is not permission for
    the project to settle a contribution dispute. Late contributions, credited years, relevant benefit years, linking
    periods, revision and supersession remain separate legal questions within the legacy regime.\n\n## Inspected
    passages\n\n- [DMG 56007, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [DMG 56008, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=7).\n\
    - [DMG 56016, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [DMG 56017, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=10).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch56`:
    PDF `24fde3944e7e2605c24baf711da1ace4dfe0032fe13b6bfc169e4562bf5ecca5`; extracted pages `b5dc3260133af75807e6248202525da77a6610befc0b7ff20bc883d2ebba530e`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.379452Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a80bf45ed915d74e623036c/dmgch56.pdf#page=7
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-revision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source directs consideration of revision or supersession after late contributions are
      treated as paid.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch56/0010
      quote: "56017   If there is an existing decision, the DM may need to consider revising or\n        superseding
        it. A change of circumstances will occur on the date it is accepted that\n        late contributions are
        treated as having been paid1. See DMG Chapter 03 for full\n        guidance on revision and DMG Chapter
        04 for full guidance on supersession.\n                                                                \
        \             1 SS (Crediting etc) Regs, regs 4-8\n\n\n\n\nVol 10 Amendment 37 June 2014"
      locator: DMG 56017
